# Dummy for Debian trixie's libglx-mesa0, the GLX vendor of libglvnd. This mesa is built without GLX; the dummy exists
# because libgl1 (pulled in by Xwayland, so by cage) would otherwise install Debian's libglx-mesa0, and that depends on
# mesa-libgallium (= 25.0.7-2+deb13u1) - exactly Debian's version, which the epoch of our dummy does not match.
# It Provides libglx-vendor, the alternative libglx0 accepts instead. rootfs/build-rootfs.sh builds this file into a
# .deb (dpkg-deb, the same fields equivs-build reads) and installs it with the base image.
Package: libglx-mesa0
Version: 1:25.0.7-2+deb13u1
Architecture: arm64
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Provides: libglx-vendor
Description: dummy for libglx-mesa0, the GLX vendor of libglvnd (none: this mesa has no GLX)
 No files. This mesa is built without GLX; the package only keeps Debian's
 libglx-mesa0 (which needs mesa-libgallium of exactly Debian's version) from
 being installed when libgl1 is pulled in, e.g. by Xwayland.
